abstract: Shangyang Fuyuantang Sheguan Bureau Zhengxinlu is an accountability register
  of a Shanghai coffin-charity bureau, recording rules, donations, receipts, expenditure
  and coffin-related business. It supports research on Qing Shanghai charity, burial
  relief and charitable accounts. Using Bodleian Libraries Sinica 691, this dataset
  provides an AI-assisted transcription of 108 images, comprising 104 numbered surfaces
  and four cover or inside-cover images, in JSON, TXT, TEI and page-by-page reading
  text with source locators, uncertain readings and unknown-length gaps. The cover
  label’s 1849 conflicts with the catalogue’s 1837 while the same catalogue XML also
  records 1849; the printing year and leaf count remain unresolved, and human double
  collation is incomplete. Version 0.1.1 applies only the specified non-blind targeted
  source corrections; it is not a newly completed independent full-book second collation.
